 Any other key is kept in `page.data` for plugins. All values are escaped when they reach HTML.
 
+## Custom slugs
+
+`slug` moves a page's output away from its file location. It must be a relative path of segments made of letters, digits, `-` and `_`, separated by `/` — no `..`, no leading `/`, no extension (`isValidSlug`, `src/paths.ts`). Anything else fails the build with a `FrontMatterError`, so a slug can never write outside the output dir. Two pages that end up at the same output path fail the build with a `DuplicateRouteError` instead of overwriting each other.
+
+Links keep using the source file: `[Promo](marketing/promo.md)` points at the page's slug automatically, and so does the navigation (which still follows the source folders).
+
